; generated-format instantiation 2026-08-08
|term[entity]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A thing whose identity is independent of its current description; persists through change.
  :dual-of @value-object
  :source-type external
  :external-equivalent close:ddd-entity
  |designation entity
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-entities-values-promises
    :anchor entity-value-object
    :projection paraphrase
    A thing whose identity is independent of its current description. It persists through change; because nothing in its content can testify to its identity, an entity's identity must be minted and maintained by convention.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:id(e) \perp desc_t(e)>
    :reading Identity is orthogonal to description-at-any-moment; hence entities require designators.
  |set-rel :kind disjoint-from :to @value-object
  |rel :kind identified-by :to @designator
  |invariant
    Any content-derived handle to an entity silently becomes a handle to a value object the moment the entity changes.
